{
  "task": "E - control run, PRCC with b and sigma_v held constant",
  "method": "Identical to task A (LHS n=2000, seed 20260816, baseline scenario, t_span=(0,1095), daily output, Marino PRCC) except that b_eff = b_sample and sigma_v_eff = 1/eip_days_sample are constants with no temperature dependence.",
  "design_contrast": "Task E differs from task A in exactly one respect: whether b and sigma_v follow the seasonal temperature cycle. Their sampled values (and hence their nominal ranges) are identical, and every other parameter enters through the same mapping, so the constant-vs-scaled contrast isolates the effect of temperature forcing on the sensitivity ranking. The static-vs-constant contrast instead isolates the effect of replacing the algebraic R0 by a dynamic output (plus the model non-linearity).",
